id: pm-gh1614
title: "GH-1614: keep typed SDK data literal across CLI sentinel inputs"
description: "GitHub https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1614 reports typed PmClient fields consuming CLI sentinels. A sandboxed current-source Node24 probe with closed stdin reproduces description '-' becoming empty and assignee 'none' being removed. Typed integrations can silently rewrite provider payloads. Audit create/update/append and separate literal typed input from explicit CLI stdin, file and clear transport syntax, retaining documented unset APIs and CLI compatibility."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T17:43:51.501Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T02:38:36.281Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-28T02:38:35.392Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-28T02:38:35.392Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Literal SDK text fields preserve sentinel spellings through create/update/append; SDK data calls do not implicitly consume stdin or read files; Explicit typed clear/unset and existing CLI transport semantics retain focused conformance tests
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "SDK mutations preserve literal values through every composed option bag. Explicit SDK-backed CLI policy retains stdin, clear tokens and repeatable aliases. Template and bulk clones now transfer policy, with documented public helpers and unchanged serialized item formats."
expected_result: Native and template-backed SDK values round-trip as data; valid CLI single and bulk transports retain their grammar; explicit unset and JSON input remain deterministic.
actual_result: "Final source passes 11,518 tests across 879 passed files and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage: 67,334 lines, 54,841 branches, 14,654 functions and 71,204 statements. Both linked test groups pass. Packed npm/Node and Bun consumers each verify both SDK entrypoints, template preservation, expanded template admission, CLI aliases and nine typed no-write refusals; actual npx/bunx execute the candidate. Typecheck, ESLint and source/import/complexity checks pass. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1616 retains all closure and review evidence; revised-head composite static and hosted checks are mandatory merge gates."
