comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T17:43:51.501Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: fresh sentinel and 1614 searches plus complete 3142-item corpus and live open/in-progress lists found no canonical GH-1614 item. Full live pm-rl4e/history confirms the older none-token migration is closed for its own accepted scope; this reproduces a new SDK boundary defect. Source reproduction ran in a new temporary project/global tracker with telemetry disabled; no real data was touched. Track as separate open SDK data-integrity work while the validated refusal/recovery delivery proceeds through review."
  "2026-10-27T18:12:31.904Z","harness:codex","Review remediation: assessed high risk/high confidence from the reproduced silent rewrites, added explicit three-part SDK/CLI conformance acceptance and180minute estimate, and linked completed pm-rl4e as related lineage. The complete repository tracker-context-quality gate now passes all47 assertions, including zero missing required active metadata and the semantic graph bounds. This is intake verification, not an implementation or closure claim."
  "2026-10-27T22:08:34.310Z","harness:codex","Grouped delivery with pm-gh1606: certify literal SDK inputs at the shared SDK mutation boundary while retaining explicit CLI decoding, typed unset directives and project field validation. Full all-status read covered3143 records without omissions; only these two implementation items are claimed. Baseline branch is current main7d85bc8c1. Add independent native-client and real transport regression controls before changing production code."
  "2026-10-27T22:22:55.719Z","harness:codex","Failing-before proof on unmodified source: the literal-data regression refuses multiple dash fields as competing stdin consumers, and a bare dash collection entry consumes stdin and reaches the unchanged30second deadline. The same native cases now pass without stdin reads. Literal provenance covers direct domain operations and SDK/MCP dispatch; CLI create/update/append/update-many adapters opt into CLI syntax.71 final focused tests pass; earlier244 core client/create/update checks and82 transport/legacy checks passed. Public SDK and command snapshots show zero classified changes. Complete source coverage is now running without source edits."
  "2026-10-27T22:28:16.683Z","harness:codex","Operational checkpoint: public pm-changelog latest2026.10.27 installs/activates successfully, with all6 package-owned commands and actions healthy. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with zero unresolved/critical/high issues,5.78percent weighted finish-error rate and zero missing error-code rows. Explicitly consented get/list probes appear as fresh pm.command spans. Independent recent telemetry shows166 matched starts/finishes, zero settled mismatches across27 observed command families, sub-second per-family mean ingestion and broker queue0/0/0. Client flush drains its1 physical entry to0. These are bounded live observations, separate from historical Release/Nightly Reliability and unreleased candidate verification."
  "2026-10-27T22:51:23.832Z","harness:codex","The initial complete run is retained as failed:11510 tests pass and7 fail across5 files, with no complete coverage receipt. Three legacy SDK focus/preview cases used parent:'none' as a clearing directive; migrate those fixture intents to explicit unset and retain a literal-parent refusal. The unchanged CLI plan fixture proves composed CLI calls also need explicit CLI provenance, now added through the existing plan-to-create policy transfer. New real CLI JSON conformance fails before repair because assignee:'none' and goal:'null' disappear; decoded JSON now carries literal provenance. The same native/CLI cases are being rerun without relaxed assertions."
  "2026-10-27T23:12:55.795Z","harness:codex","SDK boundary remediation: removed all15 new CLI-to-private-core imports instead of changing the boundary policy. Added public withCliMutationInput and withLiteralMutationInput adapters in the SDK, consumed by CLI create/update/append/update-many/plan and decoded JSON paths. They clone option bags and retain explicit literal/decoded-stdin policies without serialization. Default SDK data stays literal; an adapter can explicitly opt into CLI syntax, and explicit literal data wins when composed. SDK root/runtime exports and migration guidance are being snapshot-verified with native behavior tests."
  "2026-10-28T00:52:18.517Z","harness:codex","PR1616 review control reproduces template data loss on the reviewed head: native template creation drops explicit assignee none and comment none after an unmarked merge. The real active template-handler fixture now also checks literal none/null/dash scalar and collection values, alongside CLI legacy clearing. Fixed the merge to transfer the explicit SDK input policy onto its cloned result before normalization. Original reviewed-head full static and hosted checks completed; this revision requires fresh proof."
  "2026-10-28T01:33:38.430Z","harness:codex","The additional real CLI bulk --ac control exposed a second option-composition boundary: per-item update-many bags preserved resolved stdin fields but discarded the CLI/literal input policy. Per-row cloning now transfers both policies before calling the canonical update operation. This keeps native bulk values literal and retains valid CLI alias grammar after unconditional runtime admission. The same end-to-end control failed with a dependency_failed row and now guards the composed path."
  "2026-10-28T01:38:19.155Z","harness:codex","The bulk control additionally located policy loss in the shared stdin resolver clone, before per-row options were built. Both clone boundaries now transfer interpretation policy; the same CLI bulk acceptance-criteria control passes. Native template values, explicit unset, literal JSON, CLI stdin and legacy clearing remain covered. The expanded public PmClient CLI-policy alias control also failed before dispatch was made provenance-aware and now passes. Final focused qualification:259 tests across five complete files; direct source/import/complexity analysis reports zero violations."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T22:31:38.018Z","harness:codex","Design rationale: keep CLI transport syntax at thin adapters. Direct SDK lifecycle operations default to literal data, and unpersisted weak provenance follows internal option clones so stdin planning and legacy-clear normalization cannot reinterpret provider values. Explicit unset/clear directives remain domain operations and ordinary schema/value validation still runs. No new option flag, item field or serialized transport marker is introduced."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T18:11:16.886Z","harness:codex","After creating repository work, run the complete tracker-context-quality gate before pushing. Progressive intake still requires repository acceptance criteria, risk, confidence and estimated minutes, plus real semantic relationships; a passing gate predating the new item does not certify it."
  "2026-10-28T01:06:30.774Z","harness:codex","Input provenance follows object identity: every option merger, including template expansion, must transfer policy to cloned bags and their collection values. Round-trip semantic tests at the final creation boundary detect data loss that clone shape comparisons cannot."
